  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The Department of Education obligated $2.1B in contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The agency recorded 629 awards with an average award size of $3.4M, and obligations fell 14.9% year over year. Spending by fiscal year shows a peak at $2.7B in FY21 and FY24, with FY26 at $2.1B. The largest single NAICS category is Other Activities Related to Credit Intermediation at $960M, followed by Computer Systems Design Services at $632M. Contract types tied to student finance and IT dominate the top categories, while a handful of firms receive a large share of the dollars. ACCENTURE FEDERAL SERVICES LLC received $338M, NELNET SERVICING LLC received $294M, and MAXIMUS EDUCATION LLC received $251M. The distribution of obligations indicates concentrated spending on credit intermediation, systems design, and research and evaluation, while a set of education and IT contractors account for much of the award total. These figures reflect fiscal year to date totals and are partial for the current year.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How have Education's obligations trended year over year?",
        "body": "The Department of Education obligated $2.1B in FY26 to date, down 14.9% year over year. Obligations by fiscal year were $2.7B in FY21, $2.4B in FY22, $2.4B in FY23, $2.7B in FY24, and $2.5B in FY25. The agency has completed 629 awards so far in FY26 with an average award size of $3.4M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which contract categories and vendors dominate spending?",
        "body": "Other Activities Related to Credit Intermediation leads with $960M, followed by Computer Systems Design Services at $632M and Research and Development in the Social Sciences and Humanities at $144M. ACCENTURE FEDERAL SERVICES LLC received $338M, NELNET SERVICING LLC received $294M, and MAXIMUS EDUCATION LLC received $251M. Several other vendors and NAICS categories each hold smaller but material shares of the $2.1B total."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does Department of Education spend on contracts?",
      "a": "The Department of Education obligated $2.1B in contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The agency completed 629 awards with an average award size of $3.4M, and obligations fell 14.9% year over year."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does Education buy?",
      "a": "Education buys a mix of student finance and IT services. The top NAICS categories are Other Activities Related to Credit Intermediation at $960M, Computer Systems Design Services at $632M, and Research and Development in the Social Sciences and Humanities at $144M; other categories in the top ten include Financial Transactions Processing, Reserve, and Clearinghouse Activities at $68.9M and Other Computer Related Services at $68.3M."
    },
    {
      "q": "Who are Education's largest contractors?",
      "a": "ACCENTURE FEDERAL SERVICES LLC, NELNET SERVICING LLC, and MAXIMUS EDUCATION LLC are Education's largest contractors by obligations in FY2026 to date. ACCENTURE FEDERAL SERVICES LLC received $338M, NELNET SERVICING LLC received $294M, MAXIMUS EDUCATION LLC received $251M, and other top vendors include EDFINANCIAL SERVICES LLC at $198M and MISSOURI HIGHER EDUCATION LOAN AUTHORITY at $161M."
